IO-11: read the Barrels item of IRREGULAR cross sections

link_readXsectParams() returned as soon as it had found the transect of an
IRREGULAR line, before the code that reads Barrels, so a conduit written as
"Link IRREGULAR Tsect 0 0 0 Barrels" (the layout the GUI writes) always had
one barrel, without a message. 6.0.0 reads the value. Read it here too, with
the same check as for the other shapes. The value is assigned without a
(char) cast so that the line stays correct with IO-10's int field.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-11_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/link.c b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
index 31925e1..76925f5 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/link.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
@@ -202,6 +202,14 @@ int link_readXsectParams(char* tok[], int ntoks)
         if ( i < 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_NAME, tok[2]);
         Link[j].xsect.type = k;
         Link[j].xsect.transect = i;
+
+        // --- parse number of barrels if present (Tsect 0 0 0 Barrels)
+        if ( Link[j].type == CONDUIT && ntoks >= 7 )
+        {
+            i = atoi(tok[6]);
+            if ( i <= 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_NUMBER, tok[6]);
+            Conduit[Link[j].subIndex].barrels = i;
+        }
         return 0;
     }
 
